## Why This Is Asked

Evaluates ability to design privacy-aware, cross-region tracing at scale with per-tenant residency, data minimization, and reliable provenance.

## Key Concepts

- OTLP, OpenTelemetry, per-tenant residency
- Kafka topology, cross-region replication
- Schema evolution via registry
- Edge masking of PII, immutable storage, audit trails
- Testing: fault-injection, backpressure, drift detection

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: routeSpan(span) -> maskPII(span) -> publishRegional(span)
```

```javascript
function maskPII(span) {
  const { attributes } = span;
  if (attributes.userEmail) delete attributes.userEmail;
  if (attributes.userAgent) attributes.userAgent = 'masked';
  return span;
}
```

```javascript
function routeSpan(span, region) {
  const topic = `regional-trace-${region}`;
  kafkaProducer.send({ topic, value: JSON.stringify(span) });
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you enforce per-tenant residency if a tenant migrates regions?
- How do you validate schema evolution without breaking existing traces?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a beginner OTCA path with privacy by design, geohash-based location masking, and per-tenant residency.

## Key Concepts

- Ingest-time privacy and per-tenant opt-in

- Geohash granularity and redaction strategy

- Regional topics and date-partitioned Parquet

- End-to-end testing for privacy, QoS, and data freshness

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode for ingest
function ingest(event) {
  // redact precise coords, derive geohash4
  const hash = geohash.encode(event.lat, event.lon, 4);
  const out = {
    tenant_id: event.tenant_id,
    event_type: event.event_type,
    timestamp: event.timestamp,
    geohash4: hash,
    session_id: event.session_id
  };
  publish(out);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate audits for tenants with opt-in vs opt-out?

- How would you monitor latency and privacy violations in production?

